{"title":"Career Roadmap · Aviation Weather Observer","role":"Aviation Weather Observer","summary":"An Aviation Weather Observer observes, records, interprets, and reports atmospheric conditions that affect aircraft operations, including visibility, cloud cover, wind, temperature, pressure, precipitation, thunderstorms, and other significant weather phenomena.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Meteorology / Atmospheric Science"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"In India, exact recruitment eligibility and designation vary by employer and notification. A B.Sc. can provide the scientific foundation, but some aviation-meteorology roles may require specialised meteorological qualifications/training."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons: 2026–2046","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build atmospheric science + weather observation fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Internship/training + first operational weather role"}],[{"text":"2032–2035"},{"text":"Airport weather observation, METAR/SPECI and station operations"}],[{"text":"2035–2038"},{"text":"Senior observer / aviation meteorological technician"}],[{"text":"2038–2042"},{"text":"Aviation meteorology, forecasting support, automation"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Specialist/lead roles, aviation weather systems, training and supervision"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Atmospheric fundamentals"},{"text":"Physics, mathematics, Earth science, climatology"},{"text":"Weather observation notebook"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Meteorological observation"},{"text":"Instruments, clouds, visibility, pressure, wind, precipitation"},{"text":"Weather station project"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Aviation meteorology"},{"text":"METAR, SPECI, aviation weather hazards, synoptic charts"},{"text":"Aviation-weather project"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Operational readiness"},{"text":"Observation procedures, data quality, GIS, Python, reporting"},{"text":"Airport-weather capstone + internship"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Build the Scientific Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atmospheric composition"},{"text":"Earth–Sun relationships"},{"text":"Weather and climate"},{"text":"Basic atmospheric physics"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics fundamentals"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Environmental science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Physics is particularly important"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pressure"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Density"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Radiation"},{"text":"Convection"},{"text":"Fluid motion"},{"text":"Atmospheric stability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start observing weather"},{"type":"p","text":"Maintain a personal weather log containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Relative humidity"},{"text":"Atmospheric pressure"},{"text":"Wind speed"},{"text":"Wind direction"},{"text":"Cloud type"},{"text":"Cloud amount"},{"text":"Visibility"},{"text":"Rainfall"},{"text":"Weather phenomena"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Proof by end of Year 1","text":"A structured 6–12 month weather observation dataset."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Meteorological Observation"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important stage for an aspiring weather observer."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn meteorological instruments"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand operation and limitations of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermometer"},{"text":"Hygrometer"},{"text":"Barometer"},{"text":"Anemometer"},{"text":"Wind vane"},{"text":"Rain gauge"},{"text":"Ceilometer"},{"text":"Visibility sensor"},{"text":"Automatic Weather Station"},{"text":"Weather radar"},{"text":"Radiosonde"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn measurement quality"},{"type":"p","text":"You should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Instrument errors"},{"text":"Measurement uncertainty"},{"text":"Sensor maintenance"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Missing data"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Standard observation procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud identification"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cirrus"},{"text":"Cirrostratus"},{"text":"Cirrocumulus"},{"text":"Altostratus"},{"text":"Altocumulus"},{"text":"Stratus"},{"text":"Stratocumulus"},{"text":"Cumulus"},{"text":"Cumulonimbus"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Pay particular attention to cumulonimbus, because thunderstorms are critical aviation hazards."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Aviation Weather"},{"type":"p","text":"Now move from general meteorology to aviation-specific weather."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn METAR"},{"type":"p","text":"You should be able to understand and decode observations containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Station identifier"},{"text":"Observation time"},{"text":"Wind"},{"text":"Visibility"},{"text":"Runway visual range"},{"text":"Present weather"},{"text":"Cloud information"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Dew point"},{"text":"Altimeter/pressure"},{"text":"Significant weather"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example concept:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Wind","Visibility","Weather","Clouds","Temperature/Dew Point","Pressure"]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not merely memorise codes. Understand what each observation means operationally."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn SPECI"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand special weather reports issued when significant changes occur between routine observations."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the operational importance of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sudden visibility reduction"},{"text":"Thunderstorms"},{"text":"Strong wind changes"},{"text":"Significant cloud changes"},{"text":"Pressure changes"},{"text":"Other aviation-significant phenomena"}]}]},{"heading":"Aviation Weather Hazards","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Thunderstorms"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lightning"},{"text":"Heavy precipitation"},{"text":"Gust fronts"},{"text":"Turbulence"},{"text":"Wind shear"},{"text":"Hail"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Fog"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation fog"},{"text":"Advection fog"},{"text":"Valley fog"},{"text":"Visibility reduction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Low visibility"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mist"},{"text":"Fog"},{"text":"Haze"},{"text":"Dust"},{"text":"Smoke"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Wind hazards"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crosswinds"},{"text":"Tailwinds"},{"text":"Gusts"},{"text":"Wind shear"},{"text":"Microbursts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other hazards"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Icing"},{"text":"Turbulence"},{"text":"Hail"},{"text":"Heavy rainfall"},{"text":"Dust storms"},{"text":"Sand storms"},{"text":"Volcanic ash"},{"text":"Freezing precipitation"}]}]},{"heading":"Learn Synoptic Meteorology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand how weather systems develop and move."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"High-pressure systems"},{"text":"Low-pressure systems"},{"text":"Fronts"},{"text":"Troughs"},{"text":"Ridges"},{"text":"Cyclones"},{"text":"Anticyclones"},{"text":"Jet streams"},{"text":"Monsoon systems"},{"text":"Tropical disturbances"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to interpret:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Surface weather charts"},{"text":"Upper-air charts"},{"text":"Satellite imagery"},{"text":"Radar imagery"},{"text":"Numerical weather prediction outputs"}]}]},{"heading":"Digital & Data Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern Aviation Weather Observer should not depend entirely on manual observation."},{"type":"h","text":"GIS"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Spatial data"},{"text":"Airport mapping"},{"text":"Weather-station mapping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"p","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"├── NumPy"},{"type":"p","text":"├── pandas"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Matplotlib"},{"type":"p","text":"├── xarray"},{"type":"p","text":"└── basic geospatial libraries"},{"type":"p","text":"Use Python for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Weather-data cleaning"},{"text":"Time-series analysis"},{"text":"Temperature trends"},{"text":"Wind analysis"},{"text":"Rainfall analysis"},{"text":"Automated reports"},{"text":"Quality control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data formats"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CSV"},{"text":"JSON"},{"text":"NetCDF"},{"text":"GRIB/GRIB2"}]}]},{"heading":"Airport Meteorological Environment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the airport environment itself."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Runways"},{"text":"Taxiways"},{"text":"Aprons"},{"text":"Runway orientation"},{"text":"Airport elevation"},{"text":"Runway visual range"},{"text":"Wind measurement locations"},{"text":"Weather observation stations"},{"text":"Instrument landing systems"},{"text":"Air traffic operations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand why weather information must be accurate, timely and operationally consistent."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Airport Weather Observation"},{"text":"Routine and special weather observations"}],[{"text":"Aviation Meteorology"},{"text":"Weather impact on flight operations"}],[{"text":"Weather Instrumentation"},{"text":"Sensors, AWS and calibration"}],[{"text":"Remote Sensing"},{"text":"Radar and satellite meteorology"}],[{"text":"Severe Weather"},{"text":"Thunderstorms, wind shear, hail"}],[{"text":"Visibility Meteorology"},{"text":"Fog, haze, RVR"}],[{"text":"Weather Data Analysis"},{"text":"Python, statistics, climate/weather datasets"}],[{"text":"Airport Weather Systems"},{"text":"Automated observation systems and integration"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise internships involving:"},{"type":"h","text":"Weather stations"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meteorological observatories"},{"text":"Automatic weather stations"},{"text":"Research institutes"},{"text":"Universities with atmospheric-science laboratories"},{"text":"Environmental monitoring stations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Aviation"},{"type":"p","text":"Try to obtain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airport meteorological units"},{"text":"Aviation weather services"},{"text":"Airport operations"},{"text":"Weather instrumentation"},{"text":"Flight-weather support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Good projects include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fog prediction"},{"text":"Airport visibility analysis"},{"text":"Thunderstorm climatology"},{"text":"Wind-pattern analysis"},{"text":"Weather-data quality control"},{"text":"Urban weather effects near airports"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"Project","text":"Airport Weather Observation & Analysis System"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a system that collects weather observations and generates an aviation-oriented dashboard."},{"type":"h","text":"Inputs"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Humidity"},{"text":"Pressure"},{"text":"Wind"},{"text":"Rainfall"},{"text":"Visibility"},{"text":"Cloud information"}]},{"type":"h","text":"System"},{"type":"flow","items":["Weather Sensors / Dataset","Data Collection","Quality Control","Python Processing","Weather Analysis","Operational Dashboard"]},{"type":"h","text":"Output"},{"type":"p","text":"Display:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Current conditions"},{"text":"Wind rose"},{"text":"Visibility trend"},{"text":"Temperature trend"},{"text":"Pressure trend"},{"text":"Weather alerts"},{"text":"Historical observations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates both meteorological knowledge and operational data skills."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise recognised meteorology and aviation-related training."},{"type":"h","text":"Technical learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Build competency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation meteorology"},{"text":"Weather observation"},{"text":"METAR/SPECI"},{"text":"Synoptic meteorology"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Radar meteorology"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Additional useful areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"Numerical weather prediction"},{"text":"Satellite meteorology"},{"text":"AWS instrumentation"},{"text":"Occupational safety"},{"text":"Data quality management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not collect certificates simply for the resume. Practical observation and operational knowledge matter more."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on qualifications and employer requirements, possible roles include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Main work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Weather Observer"},{"text":"Record atmospheric conditions"}],[{"text":"Aviation Weather Observer"},{"text":"Airport-specific observations"}],[{"text":"Meteorological Technician"},{"text":"Instruments + observation systems"}],[{"text":"Weather Station Technician"},{"text":"Operate and maintain stations"}],[{"text":"Meteorological Data Analyst"},{"text":"Analyse weather datasets"}],[{"text":"Aviation Weather Support Assistant"},{"text":"Support aviation weather operations"}],[{"text":"Remote Sensing Technician"},{"text":"Radar/satellite weather data"}],[{"text":"Weather Instrumentation Technician"},{"text":"Sensors and calibration"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Some higher-level meteorologist/aviation meteorologist positions may require postgraduate or specialised meteorological qualifications."}]},{"heading":"Employer Test / Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Expect questions such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Meteorology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What causes atmospheric pressure?"},{"text":"What is atmospheric stability?"},{"text":"How are clouds formed?"},{"text":"What causes fog?"},{"text":"What is a temperature inversion?"},{"text":"What is a cyclone?"},{"text":"How does a thunderstorm develop?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Aviation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is METAR?"},{"text":"What is SPECI?"},{"text":"Why is visibility important for aviation?"},{"text":"What is runway visual range?"},{"text":"Why are crosswinds important?"},{"text":"What is wind shear?"},{"text":"Why is cumulonimbus dangerous to aircraft?"},{"text":"What is aviation icing?"},{"text":"What weather conditions affect take-off and landing?"},{"text":"How would you respond to rapidly deteriorating visibility?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Instrumentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How does an anemometer work?"},{"text":"How is atmospheric pressure measured?"},{"text":"How does a rain gauge work?"},{"text":"What is an Automatic Weather Station?"},{"text":"How would you identify a faulty sensor?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For long-term advancement, postgraduate education can significantly expand opportunities."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant PG areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Meteorology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Atmospheric Science"},{"text":"M.Sc. Applied Meteorology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Climate Science"},{"text":"M.Sc. Atmospheric Physics"},{"text":"M.Tech./M.Sc. related atmospheric/environmental disciplines"},{"text":"Remote Sensing & GIS"},{"text":"Geoinformatics"},{"text":"Climate Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful research areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation meteorology"},{"text":"Severe weather"},{"text":"Climate change"},{"text":"Numerical weather prediction"},{"text":"Atmospheric modelling"},{"text":"Satellite meteorology"},{"text":"Radar meteorology"},{"text":"Weather forecasting"}]}]},{"heading":"Government / Public-Sector Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For India, monitor recruitment and qualification requirements from organisations involved in meteorological and aviation operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential ecosystem:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"India Meteorological Department"},{"text":"Airports and airport operators"},{"text":"Civil aviation organisations"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Government weather/environment departments"},{"text":"Defence-related meteorological operations"},{"text":"Public-sector infrastructure organisations"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Government job titles and eligibility change by recruitment notification. Always verify the current notification rather than assuming that a B.Sc. alone qualifies for a particular post."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate programs include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Meteorology"},{"text":"MSc Atmospheric Science"},{"text":"MSc Aviation Meteorology"},{"text":"MSc Climate Science"},{"text":"MSc Environmental Physics"},{"text":"MSc Remote Sensing"},{"text":"MSc Earth Observation"},{"text":"MSc Atmospheric Modelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong international research directions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation weather"},{"text":"Climate modelling"},{"text":"Severe weather prediction"},{"text":"Atmospheric chemistry"},{"text":"Weather radar"},{"text":"Satellite meteorology"},{"text":"Numerical weather prediction"},{"text":"AI-based weather forecasting"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A possible progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Meteorology / Atmospheric Science","Weather Observation Trainee","Aviation Weather Observer","Senior Weather Observer","Meteorological Technician / Aviation Weather Specialist","Aviation Meteorologist / Weather Systems Specialist","Senior Specialist / Operations Lead","Manager / Technical Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Progression depends heavily on the employer, qualifications and recruitment pathway."}]},{"heading":"Technical Specialist Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For students who prefer technology over management:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Aviation Weather Observer","Meteorological Data Specialist","Weather Systems Specialist","Radar / Satellite Specialist","Weather Data / NWP Specialist","Senior Aviation Weather Technology Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Radar data"},{"text":"Satellite data"},{"text":"NetCDF"},{"text":"GRIB"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Numerical weather prediction"},{"text":"Cloud computing"}]}]},{"heading":"AI + Aviation Weather","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By the 2030s, AI will increasingly support weather observation and forecasting."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Time-series forecasting"},{"text":"Anomaly detection"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Satellite-image analysis"},{"text":"Radar-image classification"},{"text":"Automated weather-station quality control"},{"text":"Probabilistic forecasting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential projects:"},{"type":"h","text":"Airport Fog Prediction"},{"type":"flow","items":["Historical Weather","Visibility + Humidity + Temperature","Machine Learning Model","Fog Probability","Airport Weather Dashboard"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should support operational meteorologists and observers, not replace the requirement for reliable observations and human operational judgement."}]},{"heading":"Research / PhD Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For students interested in research:"},{"type":"h","text":"PhD areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric dynamics"},{"text":"Weather prediction"},{"text":"Climate modelling"},{"text":"Severe storms"},{"text":"Radar meteorology"},{"text":"Satellite meteorology"},{"text":"Atmospheric chemistry"},{"text":"AI for weather forecasting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible career destinations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Meteorological research organisations"},{"text":"Weather technology companies"},{"text":"Climate research institutions"},{"text":"Government research organisations"},{"text":"Aviation weather research"}]}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role is likely to become increasingly automated."},{"type":"p","text":"Traditional:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human","observes","records","reports"]},{"type":"p","text":"Future:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sensors","automated observation","AI quality control","human verification","operational dissemination"]},{"type":"p","text":"The valuable professional will therefore understand both atmospheric science and automated weather systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI weather forecasting"},{"text":"Digital twins of airports"},{"text":"Autonomous weather stations"},{"text":"Advanced radar"},{"text":"Satellite constellations"},{"text":"High-resolution numerical models"},{"text":"Airport micro-weather modelling"},{"text":"Real-time weather data platforms"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Core Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atmospheric science"},{"text":"Meteorology"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Synoptic meteorology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Aviation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation meteorology"},{"text":"METAR"},{"text":"SPECI"},{"text":"Visibility/RVR"},{"text":"Aviation weather hazards"},{"text":"Airport operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Observation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Weather instruments"},{"text":"AWS"},{"text":"Cloud identification"},{"text":"Weather observation"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Quality control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"Matplotlib"},{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"NetCDF/GRIB"},{"text":"Satellite/radar data"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Technical reporting"},{"text":"Operational communication"},{"text":"Data accuracy"},{"text":"Safety awareness"},{"text":"Shift-work discipline"},{"text":"Decision support"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Atmospheric science foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Weather observation + instruments"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Aviation meteorology + METAR/SPECI"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Airport-weather internship + capstone"}],[{"text":"0–2 years after UG"},{"text":"Weather Observer / Meteorological Technician pathway"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Senior Observer / Aviation Weather Specialist"}],[{"text":"5–10 years"},{"text":"Specialist / Aviation Meteorology / Weather Systems"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Technical Lead / Manager / Research Specialist"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate targeting Aviation Weather Observer should leave the B.Sc. with:"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Sc. Meteorology / Atmospheric Science + practical weather observation + METAR/SPECI knowledge + meteorological instrumentation + airport-weather exposure + Python + GIS + weather-data project + internship + strong understanding of aviation weather hazards."},{"type":"p","text":"That combination provides a much stronger foundation than having a meteorology degree alone."}]}]}